# Skill surface

**Domain shift** (new service, tool surface, operational domain) ⇒ scan `<available_skills>` by description and load matched description-gated rules **before** advising or acting; follow skills as `Use the <slug> skill` (¬ fs-read skill SOT into context).

**Cursor owns sync.** `edit(cursor-plugins/ulg-ecosystem/{skills,commands,rules} ∨ census) ⇒ run scripts/cursor/install-ecosystem-plugin.sh ∧ verify $HOME and PLUGIN_INSTALL_DESTS copies match SoT` same turn; Claude-slug bodies (`shared_sync` / uploadable `life_local`) additionally regen + upload + verify. Installed trees are copies — Reload Window is not install. `¬ ask(operator, install ∨ upload ∨ "sync the plugin")` · `¬ claim(live)` before the install/upload ran this session. `cursor_only` never uploads.

`new_or_edited(command) ⇒ unfinished until this turn quotes cmp MATCH` for that file under `$HOME/.cursor/plugins/local/ulg-ecosystem/commands/` **and** each dest in `PLUGIN_INSTALL_DESTS.txt`. Commit does not install.

| Bad | Good |
|---|---|
| Commit the command file and stop | Install, quote MATCH for that command, then commit |
| Wait for the operator to say "install the commands" | Install in the same turn |

Census slugs live in the plugin tree only — never re-add under `{repo}/.cursor/skills` or `.claude/skills`. Runbook: Use the `claude-ai-bundle-sync` skill · placement `cursor-rule-placement_ulg`.

**Work-complete finishing (last).** Install is land of the plugin copy, ¬ a substitute for the session-path commit: land (install/upload) → path-explicit commit of session paths → recycle serving processes only if MCP/tool-search descriptors changed.
